From: justririll (x1e-sleep)
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: syscon: don't take the clock of a clock provider

Imported unchanged from https://github.com/justririll/x1e-sleep
(kernel/sleep/syscon-skip-clock-of-clock-providers.patch).

The clocks of a clock provider syscon (the X1E TCSR block) are its parent
clocks. Keeping one prepared pins an RPMh XO vote and stops the SoC from
turning the crystal off in suspend.
---
diff --git a/drivers/mfd/syscon.c b/drivers/mfd/syscon.c
index 21a7fcdd2737..ee9ceca17aed 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/syscon.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/syscon.c
@@ -123,7 +123,16 @@ static struct syscon *of_syscon_register(struct device_node *np, bool check_res)
 	}
 
 	if (check_res) {
-		clk = of_clk_get(np, 0);
+		/*
+		 * The "clocks" of a clock provider (e.g. the X1E TCSR block) are
+		 * its parent clocks, not a register clock. Attaching one keeps it
+		 * prepared forever, which pins an RPMh XO vote and blocks the SoC
+		 * from turning the crystal off in suspend.
+		 */
+		if (of_property_present(np, "#clock-cells"))
+			clk = ERR_PTR(-ENOENT);
+		else
+			clk = of_clk_get(np, 0);
 		if (IS_ERR(clk)) {
 			ret = PTR_ERR(clk);
 			/* clock is optional */
